      "message": "\u003e UNCHANGED:  APTX_CHANNEL_UNCHANGED value may indicate that the caller may want to change one or more aptX Configuration values but wants the Channel Mode to remain at its existing value – this saves the API user from having to recover the current value and fill it in. A default setting when the channel configuration is unknown\n\nIt doesn\u0027t make sense that why the caller doesn\u0027t need to specify the channel mode, but how does this save API users to fill it in? The caller can only update the configuration with structure AptxAdaptiveConfiguration, but won\u0027t this make a mismatch between the caller and the receiver? Why doesn\u0027t the caller know the current channel mode?",
